cxx-vecacid: ***THE WALK ABOVE IS ONLY MEANINGFUL IF `stk()` NAMED
cxx-vecacid: `free_memory_region`.***  Read the stack first.  A crash
cxx-vecacid: at any other pc is a different bug reached by a
cxx-vecacid: different route, and for it the region chain is just
cxx-vecacid: whatever the allocator happens to hold -- a healthy
cxx-vecacid: chain printed against the wrong question is exactly
cxx-vecacid: what the 33-entry run was.

