cxx-vecacid: if that printed nothing useful, do it by hand:
cxx-vecacid:   acid 1773
cxx-vecacid:   acid: regs()
cxx-vecacid:   acid: stk()
cxx-vecacid:   acid: src(*PC)
cxx-vecacid:   acid: print(*edg_dbg_n\D, " ", *edg_dbg_cur\X, " ", *edg_dbg_prev\X)
cxx-vecacid:   acid: p = *edg_dbg_prev
cxx-vecacid:   acid: print(*p\X, " ", *(p+24)\X, " ", *(p+32)\X)
cxx-vecacid: note *table is the BUFFER and **table is entry 0; that
cxx-vecacid: chain is the REUSABLE list after a fault, not the region
cxx-vecacid: chain; and lstk()'s first argument is garbage here.
cxx-vecacid: done
